<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells ferrochromium.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells ferrochromium.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said Wednesday it sold a total of 36,000 short tons of ferrochromium to two companies, Macalloy Corp. of North Charleston, South Carolina and Metallurg International Resources of New York.</p>
<p>The sales were made under long-term contracts with an approximate total current market value of $17.8 million, the agency said.</p>
<p>Separately, the Stockpile also said it sold no vanadium pentoxide in its monthly offer.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
